To keep the design simple we will:  
* Put the resistor (R1) on the left, the LED (D1) on the right, and a single power source (VCC) on the left of the resistor.  
* Connect VCC → R1 → LED anode → LED cathode → GND.  
* Use the default orientation of the symbols; this makes pin pins line up vertically, which keeps wires short and the drawing tidy.  
* No mirroring is needed – the default mirror setting of `None` keeps the symbols in their natural orientation.

